# Linux x86_64 user service only: systemctl --user, not a rootful system service.
# See INSTALL.md before starting. Install binary at ~/.local/bin/pvisor-daemon
# and unit at ~/.config/systemd/user/pvisor-daemon.service. Copy this file to
# ~/.config/pvisor/daemon.env (chmod 600); supply all required paths and key.
# Strong random API key of at least 32 bytes, e.g. openssl rand -hex 32.
# Distinct from the HTTP OPEN-SANDBOX-API-KEY header.
OPEN_SANDBOX_API_KEY=
# Trusted local <key>.json manifests, not a registry or Podman image store.
PVISOR_DAEMON_IMAGES_DIR=/srv/pvi
# REQUIRED: existing writable delegated cgroup v2 hierarchy with enabled
# cpu/memory/pids controllers and cgroup.kill. An ordinary directory is invalid.
# Delegate= requests delegation; it does not provision this separate hierarchy.
PVISOR_DAEMON_CGROUP_ROOT=
# Short absolute private persistent directory, owned by the service user (0700).
# Provision explicitly; do not put it under a long home path or erase on restart.
# Example for one daemon only; use a unique short directory for each instance.
PVISOR_DAEMON_STATE=/var/lib/pvd
PVISOR_DAEMON_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8080
PVISOR_DAEMON_MAX_SANDBOXES=32
PVISOR_DAEMON_CPU_MILLIS=4000
PVISOR_DAEMON_MEMORY_BYTES=8589934592
# Requires usable /dev/kvm. Preflight verifies KVM and real controller writes.
# Prepared immutable rootfs must bootstrap real OpenSandbox 1.1.0 execd/egress,
# initialize/authenticate them, supervise workload argv, forward signals and reap.
# Provide byte-transparent guest AF_VSOCK CID 3 listeners on ports 44772/18080.
# Stock distro rootfs is insufficient; no bootstrap recipe is supplied or validated.
# No daemon stage/apply, checkpoints or requested network-policy enforcement.
# Loopback ports may be accessible to other local users. Authenticate guest services;
# this is not a claim of hostile multi-user isolation or full SDK conformance.
# Keep loopback binding. External/wildcard listeners require TLS at a trusted proxy
# and an explicit --public-endpoint (host:port) unit override.
# State and detached native supervisors survive daemon restarts intentionally.
# Never delete state to force cleanup. TTL cleanup is best effort while running.
